# Uclusion bootstrap for Cursor

Helpers follow only their selected complete role and bounded assignment, including instruction-source work; capsule helpers use their selected design package. They fetch current evidence and own their role actions. Never inherit dispatcher/bootstrap workflow. This changes no tools/configuration.

Only dispatchers apply the rest. The closest project bootstrap and adjacent .cursor/skills/uclusion/SKILL.md override personal/user packages: load that exact skill, never ambiguous global /uclusion or combined packages; otherwise use /uclusion.

Read the selected dispatcher and delivery bodies completely through closing markers once; reuse across Pokes. Reload known updates, incomplete reads or body loss/restoration. Root loads no semantic helper bodies or target/capsule/standing bodies to dispatch.

Resident authority: Cursor chat-owned delivery; CLI `{{UCLUSION_CLI}}`. Before every typed turn including first/return/unrelated requests, on listener output/exit before handling/rearm, and every Uclusion activation, hold selected-package references/cursor-delivery.md plus references/delivery-common.md and follow them. Never infer mode from tools/combine clients.

Before Start/Added/Updated/Responded or requests naming Uclusion/Poke AI/find_work or J-/T-/B-/Q-/S-/O-/I-/R-/C- codes, load the selected skill. Handle delivered lines in order. At unassigned startup/confirmed assignment end dispatch discovery; retained assignments discover others only on explicit human request, never Poke/rearm/turn end.

Missing/unreadable skill/reference means broken install: request permission for `{{UCLUSION_CLI}} update`, then require client restart/MCP reconnect before Uclusion work; never improvise.
